---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LegalPage from "../components/blocks/LegalPage.astro";
import { ANALYTICS } from "../lib/constants";
---
<BaseLayout locale="en" title="Cookie policy — Slow North">
  <LegalPage title="Cookie policy"
             lede="Short, because there is not much to say.">
    <h2>Before you choose, we set nothing</h2>
    <p>
      Arriving on this site sets no cookies. No analytics script is loaded, and no request
      is made to Google or any other third party. That is a deliberate choice: we use
      Google Consent Mode in its <em>basic</em> configuration rather than the “advanced”
      one, because advanced still sends cookieless pings before consent.
    </p>

    <h2>If you allow analytics</h2>
    <p>
      Google Analytics 4 loads and sets its own cookies (names beginning <code>_ga</code>)
      to count visits and see which pages are read. We grant analytics storage only.
      Advertising storage, ad personalisation and ad user data are never granted.
    </p>

    <h2>If you decline</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing loads, and we actively expire any <code>_ga</code> cookies a previous
      acceptance had set.
    </p>

    <h2>Remembering your choice</h2>
    <p>
      Your decision is stored in your browser's local storage under
      <code>{ANALYTICS.storageKey}</code>. That is a preference rather than tracking, so it
      is itself exempt from consent. We re-ask after {ANALYTICS.renewDays} days.
    </p>

    <h2>Changing your mind</h2>
    <p>
      Use <strong>Cookie preferences</strong> in the footer of any page. Withdrawing
      consent is exactly as easy as giving it, which is the legal requirement and also
      just fair.
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</BaseLayout>
